    "reason": "[ev-689bc0108c6c] says only that `tls.caOptional` \"has been removed\" from ForwardAuth and several providers. It does not say what happens to configurations that still set it. The proposed resource-rejected consequence says the field is gone from the v3.0.0 Middleware schema. The CRD validator contradicts this: it found spec.forwardAuth.tls.caOptional still in the v3.0.0 schema [ev-0842f8f3bd9d], so the rejection claim is not supported. To decide between setting-ignored and a load or validation failure, we need upstream text or code showing how v3.0.0 handles a configuration that still sets the option.",
